{
	"_comment": "Commanders and gear. Commanders lead your attacks (one per army, away until it is home); the castellan leads your castle's defence. Each wears gear in four slots, which robber barons drop when beaten: attack gear for commanders, defence gear for the castellan. Stats are percent: wall_attack (your soldiers' damage at the walls), yard_attack (in the courtyard), wall_cut (takes that share off the wall's bonus, like ladders), loot (more carried home); wall_defence (defenders' damage at the walls), yard_defence (in the courtyard), wall_bonus (the wall is that much stronger, like a moat). Every stat adds up over a commander's gear (plus per_level for each level past the first on wall_attack and yard_attack) up to `caps`. A camp of level L drops an item with chance drop_base + drop_per_level * (L - 1) (at most drop_max); its rarity is picked with weights base + per_level * (L - 1) (never below 0). Commanders gain xp by fighting: xp_win_per_level per camp level for a win, xp_player_win for beating a player, xp_loss for a lost fight; `levels` is the total xp each level needs.",
