	"_gems_comment": "Gems, Marks and the forge. Every piece of gear has `sockets` (by rarity) for gems; a gem adds its tier's `value` percent to its stat, counted with the gear's own stats (and under the same caps). A gem fits gear of its stat's side. Prising a gem out again costs `unsocket_marks` for its tier; it goes back in your pouch. `fuse` gems of one kind and tier make one of the next tier. A beaten camp of level L also drops a gem with chance gem_drop.base + gem_drop.per_level * (L - 1) (at most gem_drop.max), its tier picked with the weights in gem_drop.tiers (base + per_level * (L - 1), never below 0), its kind at random; and it gives max(1, floor(marks_per_level * L)) Marks. Marks are the trade coin: earned only by playing (beating barons, melting gear for `melt` Marks by rarity, chest jackpots, Ember Horde and tournament prizes), never bought. The forge turns `forge_count` pieces of one rarity and side into one random piece of the next rarity, in the slot of the first, for `forge` Marks by rarity (gems in them go back to your pouch).",
